# tests/findall/retry_anchor.rxt -- [FINDALL-NEXT] the find-all retry at a
# position past 0 (code review 2026-10-23-r2, CONTRACT-1): after an empty
# match at q > 0 the NOTEMPTY_ATSTART retry is an anchored attempt at q, where
# `^` and `\A` are FALSE. The DFA retry machine used to start from the
# subject-start root there and report a match `^x` cannot make. The `mg`
# counts are libpcre2 10.46's GLOBAL counts (pcre2demo.c's loop: an empty
# match retried with NOTEMPTY_ATSTART|ANCHORED, else one character on),
# hand-run per subject; python3 re.finditer agrees on every one.

pattern \x20*|^x+
features all
mg "  x" 3
mg "x x" 5

pattern |^x
features all
mg "xx" 4
mg "  x" 4
mg "x" 3

pattern |(?:^a|b)
features all
mg "aab" 6

pattern |\Ax
features all
mg "ax" 3
mg "xx" 4
mg " x" 3

pattern (?m)|^x
features all
mg "a\nx" 5
